    "solution": "Step 1: An empty set contains no elements: \\(n(A) = 0\\), denoted by \\(\\emptyset\\) or \\(\\{\\}\\).\nStep 2: Natural numbers \\(\\mathbb{N}\\) begin from 1, so there is no natural number less than 1.\nStep 3: Hence, \\(\\{x \\mid x \\in \\mathbb{N}, x < 1\\} = \\emptyset\\).",
