    "questionCode": "MH-9-MTH1-1-1.5.2-OSC-101",
    "text": "In a class, \\(35\\) students play cricket, \\(30\\) play football, and \\(15\\) play both games. How many students play at least one game?",
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "\\(65\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "\\(55\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "\\(45\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "\\(50\\)",
        "isCorrect": true
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "solution": "Step 1: Use the cardinal formula: \\(n(A \\cup B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A \\cap B)\\).\nStep 2: Substitute values: \\(n(A \\cup B) = 35 + 30 - 15\\).\nStep 3: \\(n(A \\cup B) = 65 - 15 = 50\\).",
